 on patients with this more serious form of the condition.", "NUTRITIONAL STRATEGIES IN SEVERE ACUTE PANCREATITIS:Nutritional strategies in severe acute pancreatitis are specific approaches to providing nutrition to patients with this serious condition.", "NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT IN SEVERE ACUTE PANCREATITIS:Nutritional support in severe acute pancreatitis refers to the strategies and methods used to provide adequate nutrition to patients suffering from this serious condition.", "NUTRITIONAL GUIDELINES FOR ACUTE PANCREATITIS:Nutritional guidelines for acute pancreatitis are recommendations for dietary practices aimed at improving health outcomes in affected patients.", "NUTRITIONAL OUTCOMES IN PANCREATITIS:Nutritional outcomes in pancreatitis refer", "DR. MARÍA ARGENTE PLA:A medical doctor involved in a clinical case of a diabetic patient with cystic fibrosis.", "DR. ROSA Mª MIRETE LÓPEZ:A medical doctor involved in a clinical case of a patient with diabetes mellitus and inflammatory bowel disease.", "GASTROSTOMÍA QUIRÚRGICA:A surgical procedure to create an opening into the stomach for nutritional support, particularly in patients with swallowing difficulties.", "PACIENTE CON DEMENCIA Y DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 2:A clinical case involving a patient with dementia and type 2 diabetes mellitus, discussed during the round table event.", "PACIENTE DIABÉTICO CON FIBROSIS QUÍSTICA:A clinical case involving a diabetic patient with cystic fibrosis, discussed during the round table event.", "PACIENTE CON DIABETES MELLITUS Y ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL:A clinical case involving a patient with diabetes mellitus and inflammatory bowel disease, discussed during the round table event.", "NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL EN PACIENTE DIABÉTICO CON CARCINOMA EPIDERMOIDE DE LARINGE:A clinical case involving enteral nutrition in a diabetic patient with laryngeal squamous cell carcinoma, discussed during the round table event.", "UNCYD:UNCyD, or Unidad de Nutrición Clínica y Dietética, is a clinical nutrition unit dedicated to conducting nutritional assessments and screenings, particularly for patients over the age of 65. This institution operates within a collaborative team environment, offering nutritional support tailored to patients with special needs. Through its comprehensive approach, UNCyD aims to enhance the nutritional well-being of its patients, ensuring they receive the necessary care and resources to address their specific dietary requirements."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}